  "description": "CR 702.170f plotting the top card exiles it from the library, and it is cast free later",
  "note": "Fblthp, Lost on the Range lets alice plot the top card of her library for its mana cost. She takes the action at the granted {4}{U}, which taps all five Islands where the Djinn of Fool's Fall's printed plot {3}{U} would leave one. No stack is used (CR 702.170b) and alice keeps priority (CR 116.3); the Djinn is exiled from the library (CR 702.170f), leaving the Djinn under it on top. Its cast is refused that turn and is free on turn 3 (CR 702.170d), every Island left untapped. On turn 3 the Djinn that was under it has been drawn as a new object, so the exiled one is the first live Djinn.",
